From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] 0189: SweetSurface: room for 4-row groups, so the GPU can draw into the display's buffers

Mesa's A6xx layout pads a render target's height to a multiple of 4 rows
and checks the imported memory covers it. The display's buffers on the
full-width canvas (1125 x 2250, rows of 4608) were allocated for exactly
2250 rows: 10371072 bytes against the 10377216 Mesa wants, so every import
of them failed (GL_INVALID_VALUE) and eagl copied each frame out by CPU.
A surface of one plane now gets room for whole groups of 4 rows (here 2252
rows, one more 16K page); the DPU's scanout pool is sized the same (0145).
Wrapped surfaces (0154) keep the caller's size. bluesurf_rowpad=0 turns
the padding off.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -383,6 +383,21 @@
 		s->planeCount = planes->getCount();
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * 0189: room for whole groups of 4 rows. Mesa's A6xx layout pads a render target's
+	 * height to a multiple of 4 and refuses an import whose memory is shorter: the display's
+	 * buffers (1125 x 2250, rows of 4608) were 6144 bytes short and always copied out.
+	 */
+	{
+		uint32_t rowpad = 1;
+		PE_parse_boot_argn("bluesurf_rowpad", &rowpad, sizeof(rowpad));
+		uint64_t padded = (uint64_t)s->offset + (uint64_t)s->bytesPerRow *
+		    ((sweet_div_up(s->height, s->elementHeight) + 3ull) & ~3ull);
+		if (rowpad && s->planeCount == 0 && padded > end) {
+			end = padded;
+		}
+	}
+
 	uint64_t alloc = sweet_dict_u32(props, "IOSurfaceAllocSize", 0);
 	if (alloc < end) {
 		alloc = end;
